# REST API

Dokan Kits implements a REST API for interacting with the plugin's functionality from the frontend or external applications.

## Directory Structure

- [includes/REST/](mdc:includes/REST): Main REST API code
  - [Controllers/](mdc:includes/REST/Controllers): REST API controllers
  - [Middleware/](mdc:includes/REST/Middleware): Request middleware

## REST Controllers

REST controllers extend the WordPress `WP_REST_Controller` class:

```php
namespace Dokan_Kits\REST\Controllers;

use WP_REST_Controller;
use WP_REST_Request;
use WP_REST_Response;

class MyController extends WP_REST_Controller {
    public function register_routes() {
        register_rest_route('wp-plugin-starter/v1', '/endpoint', [
            'methods' => 'GET',
            'callback' => [$this, 'get_items'],
            'permission_callback' => [$this, 'get_items_permissions_check'],
        ]);
    }

    // Controller methods...
}
```

## Registration Process

REST controllers are registered through the service provider system:

- [includes/Core/DI/Providers/RestServiceProvider.php](mdc:includes/Core/DI/Providers/RestServiceProvider.php): Registers REST controllers
- [includes/Core/Bootstrap.php](mdc:includes/Core/Bootstrap.php): Bootstraps REST API in the `boot_rest()` method

## API Namespace

All REST API endpoints use the `wp-plugin-starter/v1` namespace:

```
/wp-json/wp-plugin-starter/v1/endpoint
```

## Authentication

The REST API uses WordPress's authentication system. Most endpoints require the user to be logged in with appropriate capabilities.
